# HelioForge Energy Lab

A free hybrid-energy research and learning preview maintained by Mohammad Rezwan Khan. MKGrid serves bundled examples and bounded Terminal energy-balance calculations. Advanced studies require the separate local Python app.

- [Overview](https://mkgrid.co.technology/)
- [Browser preview](https://mkgrid.co.technology/run/)
- [Methodology and model limits](https://mkgrid.co.technology/methodology/)
- [Author, source and privacy](https://mkgrid.co.technology/about/)
- [Maintainer profile](https://mrkhan.co.technology/)
- [Full static page text](https://mkgrid.co.technology/llms-full.txt)
- [Machine-readable app facts](https://mkgrid.co.technology/app.json)
- [Public source](https://github.com/mohammadrezwankhan/helioforge-energy-lab)

## Scope
36 architectures and 36 linked lessons. In the local Python app, 19 architectures have electricity-balance screens and 17 are study-only. The Terminal workbench runs new bounded hourly energy balances, sweeps and local sensitivities. Advanced studies and optimization require the local Python app.

## Boundaries
Educational research examples, not calibrated forecasts, plant controls, investment advice or operational approval. External AI is not used by this website. Browser storage is origin-specific and does not automatically transfer from another domain.

## Separate project
[MKTrade methodology](https://mktrade.co.business/methodology/) describes a separate synthetic wind-market model. It is not a HelioForge model or validation source.

This optional text supplements the visible pages; it does not guarantee search rankings or AI citations.
